      "text": "To solve the given system of equations, we want to isolate the variable \\( x \\).\n\nLet's begin by expressing \\( y \\) in terms of \\( x \\). \n\n**Step 1: Isolate \\( y \\) for eq1**\nStarting with:\n\n$$\n3x - 5y = -11\n$$ Divide everything by -5:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x - 5y}{-5} = \\frac{-11}{-5}\n$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3x}{5} + y = \\frac{11}{5}\n$$ Add \\(\\frac{3x}{5}\\) to both sides:\n\n$$\ny = \\frac{11}{5} + \\frac{3x}{5}\n$$\n\n**Step 2: Isolate \\( x \\) for eq2**\n\nStarting with:\n\n$$\n7x + 2y = -12\n$$\nSubtract \\(2y\\) from both sides:\n\n$$\n7x = -12 - 2y\n$$\nAdd 12 to both sides:\n\n$$\n7x = -2y - 12\n$$\nDivide by 7:\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{-2y - 12}{7}\n$$\n\n**Step 3: Equate \\( y \\) and \\( x \\) expressed**\n\nRecall that the derived expressions for both \\( x \\) and \\( y \\):\n\n$$\ny = \\frac{11}{5} + \\frac{3x}{5}\n$$\n$$\nx = \\frac{-2y - 12}{7}\n$$\nObserve that \\( y \\) and \\( x \\) should be equal since we solved for each other first.\n\nCross-multiply to isolate either \\( x \\) or \\( y \\):\n\n$$\n5y = 11 + 3x\n$$\n$$\n7x = -2y - 12\n$$\n\nRewrite:\n\n$$\n3x + 7x = 11 - 12\n$$\n$$\n10x = -1\n$$\n$$\nx = -\\frac{1}{10}\n$$\n\nSubstitute \\( x \\) back to find \\( y \\):\n\n$$\ny = -\\frac{11}{5} - \\frac{3(-1)}{5}\n$$\n$$\ny = -\\frac{11}{5} + \\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n$$\ny = \\frac{-11+3}{5}\n$$\n$$\ny = \\frac{-8}{5}\n$$\n\nOur final solution is:\n$$\n\\boxed{\\left( -\\frac{1}{10}, -\\frac{8}{5} \\right)}\n$$",
